{"name":"Aged Papyrus","hex":"#ceb588","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aged","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Old.","Having the age of."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Old people, collectively."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aged"},{"term":"papyrus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant (Cyperus papyrus) in the sedge family, native to the Nile river valley, paper reed.","A material similar to paper made from the papyrus plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/papyrus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ageing","blocks":[{"text":"Ageing is the process of becoming older. The term refers mainly to humans, many other animals, and fungi; whereas for example, bacteria, perennial plants and some simple animals are potentially biologically immortal. In a broader sense, ageing can refer to single cells within an organism which have ceased dividing, or to the population of a species."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ageing"},{"title":"Papyrus","blocks":[{"text":"Papyrus is a substance used in ancient times as a writing surface. Similar to thick paper, it was first known to have been used in Egypt as the papyrus plant from which it was created was once abundant across the Nile Delta. Papyrus was made from the pith of the papyrus plant, Cyperus papyrus, a wetland sedge. Papyrus can also refer to a document written on sheets of such material, joined side by side and rolled up into a scroll, an early form of a book."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Papyrus.jpg/330px-Papyrus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papyrus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wi